WEBVTT

NOTE
This file was generated by Descript <www.descript.com>

00:00:01.090 --> 00:00:03.970
Leah: Let’s look at how adults
and parents can help children and

00:00:03.970 --> 00:00:07.300
young people make good lifestyle
choices to help with Self Esteem.

00:00:07.800 --> 00:00:11.980
Rhiannon: If a child or young person
feels unimportant or worthless, it

00:00:11.980 --> 00:00:15.979
will likely lead to sad emotions
and create poor self-esteem.

00:00:18.299 --> 00:00:21.630
This is a common factor in children
and young people experimenting

00:00:21.630 --> 00:00:25.580
with alcohol or drugs and other
destructive or risky behaviours.

00:00:25.680 --> 00:00:31.069
Having strong self-esteem is essential
as a child or young person grows up, as

00:00:31.070 --> 00:00:35.009
they will face many challenges and having
a healthy self-esteem is fundamental

00:00:35.230 --> 00:00:37.450
in making safe and healthy choices.

00:00:38.390 --> 00:00:42.350
a child or young person should be
shown lots of love and positivity and

00:00:42.350 --> 00:00:44.240
told why they are special as a person.

00:00:47.690 --> 00:00:50.209
Children and young people
remember the positive things

00:00:50.299 --> 00:00:51.790
and they make them feel loved.

00:00:52.430 --> 00:00:56.340
Leah: An adult or parent who shows
positivity, when faced with challenges

00:00:56.340 --> 00:01:00.550
can implant that on a child or young
person and show them how to handle

00:01:00.550 --> 00:01:02.510
themselves when they too are challenged.

00:01:03.019 --> 00:01:06.830
They can also learn to not be afraid
to show opinions and ideas and it’s

00:01:06.860 --> 00:01:10.890
ok to disagree sometimes as long as
They consider the opinions of others.

00:01:11.770 --> 00:01:15.380
Rhiannon: All children and young people
need verbal discipline from time to time,

00:01:15.820 --> 00:01:20.020
but if the criticism is directed at the
child as a person, rather than being

00:01:20.020 --> 00:01:24.480
directed at their inappropriate behaviour
or actions, it can have a negative effect,

00:01:24.730 --> 00:01:27.040
causing them to feel ridiculed or ashamed.

00:01:28.199 --> 00:01:31.880
A parent should approach their role in
this aspect of their child’s development

00:01:32.120 --> 00:01:36.990
by acting as a life coach or a teacher,
rather than a disciplinarian or punisher.

00:01:40.050 --> 00:01:43.220
If a parent is unhappy with their
behaviour, they should tell them,

00:01:43.520 --> 00:01:45.360
but make clear they still love them.

00:01:46.420 --> 00:01:49.860
Leah: When an adult is commenting on,
or correcting the behaviour of a child

00:01:49.860 --> 00:01:54.280
or young person, it is important that
they are fair and firm, as this will

00:01:54.280 --> 00:01:58.240
help the child or young person to accept
responsibility for their bad behaviour.

00:01:59.039 --> 00:02:02.030
All children need to accept
responsibility for their behaviour,

00:02:02.580 --> 00:02:05.880
and learning self-discipline is a
very important part of growing up.

00:02:06.910 --> 00:02:11.440
Rhiannon: Valuing effort over perfection
can encourage Children and young people

00:02:11.470 --> 00:02:15.939
to take on new challenges and by not
being over-anxious about success,

00:02:16.240 --> 00:02:20.250
they might try more activities and
set themselves more goals and plans

00:02:20.259 --> 00:02:22.030
for things they’d like to accomplish.

00:02:22.609 --> 00:02:26.950
Also getting praise for any improvements
or successes can help even more.

00:02:28.010 --> 00:02:31.850
Leah: Children and young people need to be
guided to make good lifestyle changes for

00:02:31.850 --> 00:02:33.600
the benefits of their mental well-being.

00:02:34.090 --> 00:02:37.079
This could involve encouraging
them to discover and develop their

00:02:37.080 --> 00:02:41.819
talents, through clubs, groups and
activities or to express themselves

00:02:41.820 --> 00:02:44.470
creatively, through art, drama or music.

00:02:45.180 --> 00:02:48.810
finding something they are good at can
provide a huge boost to their feelings

00:02:48.810 --> 00:02:50.800
of self-worth and their self-esteem.

